    "# Question 3 — One-Variable Gradient Descent\n",
    "\n",
    "The function is\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "f(x)\n",
    "=\n",
    "x^4-\\frac83x^3-6x^2+6.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Its derivative is\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "f'(x)\n",
    "=\n",
    "4x^3-8x^2-12x\n",
    "=\n",
    "4x(x-3)(x+1).\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Gradient descent uses\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\boxed{\n",
    "x_{k+1}\n",
    "=\n",
    "x_k-\\eta f'(x_k).\n",
    "}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "For each part, we perform **100 updates** from the given $$x_0$$, so the result is $$x_{100}$$.\n",
    "\n",
    "The PDF provides a check:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "x_0=4,\\qquad \\eta=0.001\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "should produce\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "x_{100}=3.0044144797293426\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "and\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "y_{100}=f(x_{100})\n",
    "=\n",
    "-38.99953149354378.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "The code below reproduces that check."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "ea4f56c6",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def f3(x):\n",
    "    return x**4 - (8/3)*x**3 - 6*x**2 + 6\n",
    "\n",
    "def df3(x):\n",
    "    return 4*x**3 - 8*x**2 - 12*x\n",
    "\n",
    "def gradient_descent_1d(x0, eta, steps=100):\n",
    "    current = float(x0)\n",
    "\n",
    "    for k in range(steps):\n",
    "        current = current - eta * df3(current)\n",
    "\n",
    "    return current, f3(current)\n",
    "\n",
    "check_x, check_y = gradient_descent_1d(4, 0.001, 100)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Assignment check:\")\n",
    "print(\"x100 =\", check_x)\n",
    "print(\"y100 =\", check_y)"
   ]
  },
