    "# Question 10 — Derive the Dual Using Lagrange Duality\n",
    "\n",
    "The primal problem is\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\max_{(x,y)^T\\in\\mathbb{R}^2}\n",
    "\\;\n",
    "5x+3y\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "subject to\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\begin{pmatrix}\n",
    "2&2\\\\\n",
    "2&-4\\\\\n",
    "-2&1\\\\\n",
    "0&-1\\\\\n",
    "0&1\n",
    "\\end{pmatrix}\n",
    "\\begin{pmatrix}\n",
    "x\\\\y\n",
    "\\end{pmatrix}\n",
    "\\le\n",
    "\\begin{pmatrix}\n",
    "33\\\\8\\\\5\\\\-1\\\\8\n",
    "\\end{pmatrix}.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "The source explicitly places $$(x,y)$$ in $$\\mathbb{R}^2$$, so the primal variables are unrestricted in sign.\n",
    "\n",
    "Let\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_5\\ge0.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "For a maximization problem with constraints\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "Az\\le b,\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "use the Lagrangian\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "L(z,\\lambda)\n",
    "=\n",
    "c^Tz+\\lambda^T(b-Az).\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Here,\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "z=\n",
    "\\begin{pmatrix}\n",
    "x\\\\y\n",
    "\\end{pmatrix},\n",
    "\\qquad\n",
    "c=\n",
    "\\begin{pmatrix}\n",
    "5\\\\3\n",
    "\\end{pmatrix}.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Expanding,\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "L\n",
    "=\n",
    "33\\lambda_1\n",
    "+8\\lambda_2\n",
    "+5\\lambda_3\n",
    "-\\lambda_4\n",
    "+8\\lambda_5\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "+\n",
    "x\n",
    "\\left(\n",
    "5-2\\lambda_1-2\\lambda_2+2\\lambda_3\n",
    "\\right)\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "+\n",
    "y\n",
    "\\left(\n",
    "3-2\\lambda_1+4\\lambda_2-\\lambda_3+\\lambda_4-\\lambda_5\n",
    "\\right).\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Because $$x$$ and $$y$$ are unrestricted, the supremum over $$x,y$$ is finite only when their coefficients are zero.\n",
    "\n",
    "Therefore,\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "2\\lambda_1+2\\lambda_2-2\\lambda_3=5,\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "and\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "2\\lambda_1-4\\lambda_2+\\lambda_3-\\lambda_4+\\lambda_5=3.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "The dual program is therefore\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\boxed{\n",
    "\\begin{aligned}\n",
    "\\text{minimize }&\n",
    "33\\lambda_1\n",
    "+8\\lambda_2\n",
    "+5\\lambda_3\n",
    "-\\lambda_4\n",
    "+8\\lambda_5\\\\\n",
    "\\text{subject to }&\n",
    "2\\lambda_1+2\\lambda_2-2\\lambda_3=5,\\\\\n",
    "&\n",
    "2\\lambda_1-4\\lambda_2+\\lambda_3-\\lambda_4+\\lambda_5=3,\\\\\n",
    "&\n",
    "\\lambda_i\\ge0,\\qquad i=1,\\ldots,5.\n",
    "\\end{aligned}\n",
    "}\n",
    "$$"
   ]
  },
