    "# Question 13 — Two Red and Two Blue Balls\n",
    "\n",
    "There are four individual balls:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "R_1,\\;R_2,\\;B_1,\\;B_2.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Choose two without replacement.\n",
    "\n",
    "The six equally likely unordered pairs are:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "R_1R_2,\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "R_1B_1,\\;R_1B_2,\\;R_2B_1,\\;R_2B_2,\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "B_1B_2.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "We are told that **at least one ball is blue**.\n",
    "\n",
    "This removes the red-red outcome, leaving 5 possible pairs.\n",
    "\n",
    "Only one of those five is blue-blue:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "B_1B_2.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Therefore,\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\boxed{\n",
    "P(\\text{both blue}\\mid\\text{at least one blue})\n",
    "=\n",
    "\\frac15.\n",
    "}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "So the probability that the “other” ball is also blue, under the stated event that at least one is blue, is\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\boxed{\\frac15}.\n",
    "$$"
   ]
